062 #uuid "ef3410b5-607f-5268-83e7-58a7aeef5936" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120903 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120904 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120904 #edb/ref 1061 445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120904 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "213f9703-950a-5e68-9e6e-75e4744f5178" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120904 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120905 #edb/ref 1061 448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120905 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2b405cc4-9d67-53b0-94ff-33f5133c2609" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120905 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120911 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120911 #edb/ref 1061 451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120911 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "de1bdae6-79f1-521f-90b6-f0f8755e4df7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120911 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121006 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to calculate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x \\rightarrow 0} \\dfrac{x^3-2x}{x^2+4x}\n$$\n\nIf we try to evaluate the limit by directly substituting $x=0$, we get a confusing result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 0)\\frac{x^{3} - 2x}{x^{2} + 4x} &= ((0)^{3} - 2(0))/((0)^{2} + 4(0)) = \\frac{0}{0}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 0 0\n$$\n\nis called an **indeterminate form** because we are unable to determine the value of the limit from this expression.\n\nHowever, if we simplify the fraction before evaluating the limit, we obtain a more clear result. To simplify the fraction, we can factor the numerator and denominator and then cancel out any common factors.\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel} \\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{x^3-2x}{x^2+4x} & = \\dfrac{x(x^2-2)}{x(x+4)} \\\\[5pt] & = \\dfrac{\\cancel{x}(x^2-2)}{\\cancel{x}(x+4)} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac{x^2-2}{x+4} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the limit of the simplified fraction.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\lim_{x \\rightarrow 0} \\dfrac{x^3-2x}{x^2+4x} &= \\lim_{x \\rightarrow 0} \\dfrac{x^2-2}{x+4} \\\\ & = \\dfrac{(0)^2-2}{(0)+4} \\\\ & = \\dfrac{-2}{4} \\\\ & = -\\dfrac{1}{2} \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121006 #edb/ref 1065 246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121006 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "358e387e-1f79-5799-a6bc-d9a94fd46dd9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121006 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517476 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517476 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517476 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517476 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518293 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517476 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517476 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating Limits of Rational Functions by Factoring" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517476 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186518250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517476 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517476 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517476 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "1e5bf916-4dc8-5981-8525-b54be92da138" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517542 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517542 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517542 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1f3291a2-9375-59ea-b11b-d3d51ab51141" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517547 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517547 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517547 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "21831e57-25de-5c6c-9c6c-ab43447a6e8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517562 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{16}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517562 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592